  "lean": {
    "statement": "∀ {E : Type u_1} [inst : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_1 : InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [inst_2 : CompleteSpace E]\n  [inst_3 : FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [inst_4 : MeasurableSpace E] [inst_5 : BorelSpace E] {U : E → ℝ} {α β : NNReal},\n  0 < α →\n    α ≤ β →\n      ContDiff ℝ 2 U →\n        (∀ (x v : E), ↑α * ‖v‖ ^ 2 ≤ ((fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x) v) v ∧ ((fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x) v) v ≤ ↑β * ‖v‖ ^ 2) →\n          ∀ {η τ r : ℝ},\n            0 ≤ η →\n              0 < τ →\n                0 ≤ r →\n                  ∀ (ν : MeasureTheory.Measure E) [MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure ν],\n                    (InfSet.sInf\n                              {r |\n                                ∃\n                                  γ ∈\n                                    {γ |\n                                      γ.fst = ν ∧\n                                        γ.snd =\n                                          MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun p => p.1 + p.2)\n                                            ((MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace.volume.tilted fun x => -U x).prod\n                                              (MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => √η • z)\n                                                (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E)))},\n                                  r = ∫⁻ (z : E × E), ENNReal.ofReal (‖z.1 - z.2‖ ^ 2) ∂γ} ^\n                            (1 / 2)) ^\n                          2 ≤\n                        ENNReal.ofReal (r ^ 2) →\n                      have d := ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E);\n                      have M := 4 * ↑β * d + 4 * ↑β ^ 2 * η * d + 2 * ↑β ^ 2 * r ^ 2;\n                      have F := fun y z x => U x + ‖x - (y + √τ • z)‖ ^ 2 / (2 * (η + τ));\n                      MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun y => ‖gradient U y‖ ^ 2) ν ∧\n                        ∫ (y : E), ‖gradient U y‖ ^ 2 ∂ν ≤ M ∧\n                          (∀ (y z : E), gradient (F y z) y = gradient U y - (√τ / (η + τ)) • z) ∧\n                            MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun p => ‖gradient (F p.1 p.2) p.1‖ ^ 2)\n                                (ν.prod (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E)) ∧\n                              ∫ (p : E × E), ‖gradient (F p.1 p.2) p.1‖ ^ 2 ∂ν.prod (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E) =\n                                  ∫ (y : E), ‖gradient U y‖ ^ 2 ∂ν + τ * d / (η + τ) ^ 2 ∧\n                                ∫ (p : E × E),\n                                      ‖gradient (F p.1 p.2) p.1‖ ^ 2 ∂ν.prod (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E) ≤\n                                    M + τ * d / (η + τ) ^ 2 ∧\n                                  (β = 1 →\n                                    η ≤ 1 / 4 →\n                                      ∫ (p : E × E),\n                                          ‖gradient (F p.1 p.2) p.1‖ ^ 2 ∂ν.prod (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E) ≤\n                                        5 * (d + r ^ 2 + τ * d / (η + τ) ^ 2))",
    "statement_sha256": "3c250c7cfa2573a5b94183c5e2515caf3a3fc2514a77a54056d22cb127801313",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "NNReal denotes nonnegative reals, upward arrows are coercions. Module.finrank is real vector-space dimension. ContDiff R 2 is C2 regularity; fderiv is the genuine Frechet derivative and gradient the real inner-product gradient.",
      "The infimum and its lintegral cost are in ENNReal, the extended nonnegative reals. The displayed exponent (1/2) on that infimum is real-exponent ENNReal rpow; its outer exponent 2 is natural-number power. ENNReal.ofReal maps real x to max(x,0) as an extended nonnegative real.",
      "gamma.fst and gamma.snd are pushforward marginal measures. Measure.map denotes pushforward; Measure.prod denotes the actual product measure. ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E is the centered standard Gaussian probability on the finite-dimensional real inner-product space, with identity covariance.",
      "The canonical volume is Lebesgue volume for the finite-dimensional inner-product space. For arbitrary base measure mu and real function f, Mathlib defines mu.tilted f as mu.withDensity(fun x => ENNReal.ofReal(exp(f(x))/(integral y,exp(f(y)) dmu))). Nonintegrable Bochner integrals are assigned zero; real division by zero is zero. This is generic definition context, not an added integrability or normalization hypothesis.",
      "Integrable denotes actual Bochner integrability under the specified measure. The displayed real integrals are Bochner integrals, and the nonnegative integral is the extended Lebesgue integral. Real.sqrt denotes the nonnegative square root, with Mathlib real-domain conventions.",
      "Displayed have bindings in the theorem type are local let bindings. The variables y,z are fixed parameters when taking gradient of F y z with respect to its final argument. BorelSpace identifies the measurable structure with the topology.",
      "The compiled theorem type has been definitionally expanded; local project definition names are removed. This context supplies only mathematical and library definitions, no source identity or additional theorem conclusion."
    ]
